.TH HRD 6 "April 25, 2004" "hrd v0.1" "HuaRongDao Game Manual"
.\" Please adjust this date whenever revising the manpage.
.SH NAME
hrd \- the puzzle game: HuaRongDao
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hrd
[pattern]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the RuaRongDao game with the "pattern" if one is given at the 
command line, otherwise run the game with the default pattern.
See the \fBPATTERN\fP section below for more information.
.PP
HuaRongDao is an ancient Chinese game.  The rules are very easy to
understand, but the game is not so easy to solve.
.PP
The aim of the game is to move pieces in order to free the largest
one from the bottom side of the board, with as few steps as possible.  
You may not make one piece jump over another, nor can any two
pieces overlap.  Continuously moving one piece is counted as a single
step.
.SH USAGE
The following commands are supported by this program.
.TP
.B 0-9
Mark the desired piece selected.  The peice is then moved by
one or two direction letter:
.B l
for LEFT,
.B r
for RIGHT,
.B u
for UP, or
.B d
for DOWN. Normally the arrow keys can also be used as the
direction command.
.TP
.B q
Quit the game.
.TP
.B u
Undo one step.
.TP
.B r
Redo one step.
.TP
.B b
Save a bookmark.  A single letter is prompted as the bookmark slot,
valid bookmarks are \fBa-z\fP, \fBA-Z\fP, or \fB0-9\fP.
.TP
.B l
Load from a bookmark.  A bookmark slot is prompted.
.PP
\fBCtrl-C\fP can be used to cancel the current command.  
\fBENTER\fP can be used to reset the prompt and echo area.
.PP
\fBCtrl-L\fP can be used to redraw the screen.
.SH PATTERN
A pattern can be encoded as a string.  Each grid of the board is
encoded as a letter.  Each row is followed by a \fBdot\fP.
.TP
.B
Q
To indicate a big square.
.TP
.B
L R
To indicate the left and the right of a horizontal rectangle respectively.
.TP
.B
T B
To indicate the top and the bottom of a vertical rectangle respectively.
.TP
.B
P
To indicate a small square.
.TP
.B
_
To indicate an empty grid.
.PP
The dafault pattern can be encoded as \fBTQQT.BQQB.TLRT.BPPB.P__P\fP.
.SH FILES
.TP
.IB $XDG_DATA_HOME/hrd/bookmark (~/.local/share/hrd/bookmark when XDG_DATA_HOME is not set; an existing ~/.hrd/bookmark is used while that folder does not exist)
The bookmark file.
.SH BUGS
Usage of Ctrl-Z to suspend of this program is not supported (yet).
